-- title:
--   Integrality of the H₁ moduli ring over unramified constants
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a positive integer $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero containing a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity $\xi$ admitting a ring embedding $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\xi = e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell$, and let $K \subseteq L((T))$ be the intermediate field generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of the function field over $\mathbb{Q}$ of $X_{H_1}$ of level $q^2M'$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ and $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$, and let $j \in K$, assumed nonzero, have Laurent expansion the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant. Let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation ring with $\mathfrak{m}_{A_0} = (q)$, sitting under $A$ and $K$ compatibly, with $A$ finite over $A_0$, and let $\zeta_A \in A$ have image a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $L$ and generate $A$ over $A_0$; assume $A_0$ contains a primitive $\ell$-th root of unity and that $\ell$ and $M'$ are units in $A_0$. Assume further: stability of the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-point condition [`ModularCurve.IsGamma1Point`](def/ModularCurve_WeierstrassGamma1Pow.html#L10) under variable change of the level datum, stability of the cyclic-kernel condition [`ModularCurve.IsGamma0PowAt`](def/ModularCurve_WeierstrassGamma0Pow.html#L55) under [`ModularCurve.kernelVariableChangeDeg`](def/ModularCurve_WeierstrassLevelComponents.html#L104), and stability of divisibility of [`ModularCurve.inLineMulPoly`](def/ModularCurve_WeierstrassH1Pow.html#L18) under variable change; a family of relative group laws $\mathcal{G}$ on the projective Weierstrass models over $A_0$-algebras which is chord–tangent and has the origin as identity section; a level transport $\mathcal{T}$ for Drinfeld $q$-bases which is a section transport; and, for every $A_0$-algebra, the existence of graded ring homomorphisms of the projective coordinate rings realising variable changes and coefficient maps, nondegenerate on the irrelevant ideals. Let $P_0$ be a fine moduli package over $A_0$ for the moduli datum attached to `rigidDataH1Pow A₀ ℓ M' q` (a $\Gamma_0$-power kernel tuple, a $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-point, a Drinfeld $q$-basis, and the linking divisibility), and let $x$ be a point of that moduli problem over $K$ whose $j$-invariant has Laurent expansion [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18). Then the representing ring $P_0.B_0$ is an integral domain.
--
--   This is the irreducibility statement for the fine moduli ring of the guarded $H_1$ level datum over constants in which $q$ is unramified: in contrast with the situation over $A$, where the Weil pairing of the Drinfeld basis splits the ring into $q-1$ pieces, the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-point contributes no $\mu_\ell$-valued invariant and the ring stays integral. It feeds the description of the minimal primes of the moduli ring as generated by differences $b - \operatorname{alg}(\cdot)$ in the following step of the level structure analysis.
